# Example WSLVault KV v2 secret at kv/fishers/ios
# (https://vault.workstation.co.uk — same vault as kv/fishers/<ring>/config).
#
# Store these fields in Vault — never commit real values.
# Seed helper: ./ci/seed-ios-vault.sh
#
# Same names work as GitHub Actions secrets (fallback when Vault is empty).
# How to obtain each value: docs/IOS_RELEASE.md § "App Store Connect — where
# the ASC values come from".
#
#   ASC_KEY_ID              App Store Connect API Key ID (Integrations → API)
#   ASC_ISSUER_ID           Issuer ID at the top of that same page
#   ASC_PRIVATE_KEY_B64     base64(AuthKey_XXXXXX.p8) — download once from ASC
#   APPLE_TEAM_ID           10-char Apple Developer team id
#   CERT_PRIVATE_KEY_B64    base64(distribution private key .pem) # optional
#   APP_STORE_APP_ID        numeric App Store Connect app id      # optional
#   GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID    overrides the brand's own client id   # optional
#   GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID  overrides the derived URL scheme   # optional
#
# The Google ids no longer belong here. They come from
# mobile.googleIosClientId in brands/<id>.yaml, which the brand generator
# writes into brand.xcconfig — per brand, because the reversed form is a URL
# scheme in Info.plist and a shared default shipped Fishers' scheme inside
# Gully Cricket. Set them here only to override the brand's pair for one
# build; the reversed form is derived when omitted.
#
# Quick base64 of the .p8:
#   macOS:  base64 -i AuthKey_XXXXXX.p8 | tr -d '\n'
#   Linux:  base64 -w0 AuthKey_XXXXXX.p8
#
# Fishers iOS CI does not use vault.diytaxreturn.co.uk.
